{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1145069-other-pantheon-names","id":1145069,"title":"Other Pantheon Names","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-09-28T20:04:21-07:00","id":1145069,"title":"Other Pantheon Names","content":"I'm considering what the names of different cultures' pantheons might be. Obviously 2E makes this largely easier, because when it doubt you can always default to the word for &quot;gods&quot; in the given language.<br /> <br /> Ones we know...<br /> <br /> Aesir - Norse<br /> Deva - Indian<br /> Kami - Japanese<br /> Loa - Afro-Carribean<br /> Manitou - Algonquin<br /> Nemetondevos - Gaulish<br /> Netjer - Egyptian<br /> Orisha - Yoruba<br /> Palas - Vajrayana Buddhist (not 100% confirmed, but pretty obvious now that their Pantheon purview has been referenced)<br /> Plant Don - Welsh<br /> Shen - Chinese<br /> Teotl - Aztec<br /> Theoi - Greek<br /> Tuatha de Danann - Irish<br /> Yazata - Persian<br /> <br /> Ones to speculate about (a few might be confirmed and I'm forgetting). Some of these were used by John's Scion Resource, but they were chosen pretty straight forwardly based on the originating languages...<br /> <br /> Abosom - Ashanti<br /> Alihah - Arabian<br /> Alusi - Igbo<br /> Anga - Guarani<br /> Anunna - Mesopotamian<br /> Apu - Inca<br /> Atua - Polynesian (Mostly focusing on Hawiian and/or Maori probably)<br /> Bogovi - Slavic Russian<br /> Di Indigetes - ascended Roman born Scions of the Theoi<br /> Dievai - Slavic Baltic<br /> Diwata - Tagalog (with some broader Philippines overlap)<br /> Diyin Dine'e - Navajo/Apachean<br /> Elohim - Phoenician/Canaanite<br /> Hyangs - Javanese/Bali<br /> Inue - Inuit<br /> Jainko - Basque<br /> Jumalat - Finnish<br /> Kachina - Hopi/Puebloan<br /> K'uh - Mayan<br /> Lubaale - Baganda<br /> Milungu - Nyanga<br /> Nat - Burmese (credit to Svarogg for their write up of this sub-pantheon of the Deva with distinct members)<br /> Narts - Ossetian<br /> Ngen - Mapuche<br /> Numina - adopted Sabine gods of the Romans<br /> Nunnehi - Cherokee<br /> Onkulunkulu - Zulu<br /> Pangool - Serer<br /> Sga'na Qeda's - Haida<br /> Shilombish - Choctaw<br /> Shiunesh/Thousand Gods of Hatti - Hittite<br /> Sinduel - Korean<br /> Th\u1ea7n - Vietnamese<br /> Tjukuritja - Anangu<br /> Tngri - Mongolian/Turkic<br /> Wakanpi - Dakota/Lakota/Nakota<br /> Zemis - Taino","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 11-23-2017, 01:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-28T20:22:27-07:00","id":1145074,"title":"","content":"A correction:<br /> Wakanpi - Lakota (Wakan Tanka is the Great Spirit, while the Wakanpi are all other divinities, including heroes and healers)<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Religions Academic. Zoroastrian Convert.</i><br /> <b>Official Work:</b> Scion: Companion, Scion: Demigod.<br /> <b>Nexus Work:</b> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/293097/The-Cortes-Divinas-of-Maria-Lionza?cPath=8329_32938\" target=\"_blank\">Cortes Divinas of Maria Lionza</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/17311-xhepablo","name":"xhepablo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar17311_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-28T20:28:59-07:00","id":1145076,"title":"","content":"Ah! I was using &quot;Wakan Tanka&quot; in the older sense of &quot;Great Mystery&quot; that includes all spiritual beings, as the &quot;Great Spirit&quot; concept is believed to be younger for the Plains than for the Algonquins according to my reading on the subject.<br /> <br /> But you are right - Wakanpi is clearer and avoids the debate alltogether! I will change it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-28T20:47:54-07:00","id":1145081,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1145069-other-pantheon-names#post1145069\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Inuit (or Haida; I lean toward focusing further north on the Inuit, but Watcher's done great work with the Haida; there's so much overlap its unlikely for both to appear as separate... then again Tuatha de Danann and the Plant Don may beg to differ...)</div> </div> </div> </div>The Haida name for the Pantheon would be &quot;Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s&quot; which means 'Supernatural Beings' which they classify all of the figures we would see as Deities as. I don't think there would be much issue of overlap at all there, assuming the old GBN research on the Inuit Pantheon is all accurate and whatnot. Was there anything fiddly going on there? All I know about Inuit religious traditions is from GBN.<br /> <br /> There is also the Hittite Pantheon who are the &quot;Thousand Gods of Hatti,&quot; who the Hittites regarded as a different group of Gods than their neighboring peoples worshiped such as the Egyptians and Akkadians. (though they totally nicked a lot of spare Deity-change off the Mesopotamians here and there) &quot;Shiunesh,&quot; is the term for a God too if that's helpful.<br /> <br /> What's really fun with the Irish is you could probably work out what they would call most other Pantheons just by fiddling with the format of their own title. I don't know how to decline names in Old Irish yet, but when I do I'll spin a few of those together for fun.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-28T21:03:07-07:00","id":1145085,"title":"","content":"I don't know how the Olympians will respond to being called the Tuatha de Kronou...<br /> <br /> Maybe Tuatha de Rheae would be ok though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-28T21:16:45-07:00","id":1145088,"title":"","content":"I think I leapt too fast to a conclusion of overlap based on Kaiti and Nanook together with Yaahl and Tulugaq (the latter of whom is definitely a multipatheon figure like his southerly counterpart Coyote who is in the Diyin Dine'e, the Kachina... possibly the Wakanpi as well if on grounds of language that umbrella covers the Crow Nation as well). So I adjusted the list accordingly with Sga'na Qeda's added to the suggested names, and Inuit still needing one (the only name I've seen used by a fan writer before was Unipkaaqs, but that specifically refers to the stories themselves).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-29T01:26:00-07:00","id":1145129,"title":"","content":"Inuit - Shaman/ Eskimo, though Eskimo is only one race in this region...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1837-wickedgrail","name":"Wickedgrail","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1837_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-29T01:43:02-07:00","id":1145132,"title":"","content":"There's Th\u00e1nh for the Vietnamese pantheon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Pantheon(s):<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1LMQFZLq3NrOHs2cp7OWnfukuHCNI4h_0/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Nat, the Spirits of Myanmar</a><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1WDvOmQCR3a25WbVowfe8KgGbGLU0yzX3/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Phi, the Spirits of the Tai People</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13670-svarogg","name":"Svarogg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13670_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-29T02:16:11-07:00","id":1145141,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Watcher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1145069-other-pantheon-names?p=1145081#post1145081\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What's really fun with the Irish is you could probably work out what they would call most other Pantheons just by fiddling with the format of their own title. I don't know how to decline names in Old Irish yet, but when I do I'll spin a few of those together for fun.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know if Old Irish is like Modern Irish in this regard, but for some of the Pantheons either Lucht or Mu\u00edntir might be more appropriate than Tuatha. In Modern Irish there is only words for the Greco-Roman gods.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3326-an-fhuiseog","name":"An Fhuiseog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3326_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"271"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-29T04:14:27-07:00","id":1145160,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wickedgrail</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1145069-other-pantheon-names?p=1145129#post1145129\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Inuit - Shaman/ Eskimo, though Eskimo is only one race in this region...</div> </div> </div> </div>Do either of those words refer to divinities themselves?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-29T04:19:59-07:00","id":1145162,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1145069-other-pantheon-names?p=1145160#post1145160\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Do either of those words refer to divinities themselves?</div> </div> </div> </div>should they? if not Eskimo only refers to a race.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1837-wickedgrail","name":"Wickedgrail","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1837_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-29T04:20:17-07:00","id":1145163,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Svarogg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1145069-other-pantheon-names?p=1145132#post1145132\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's Th\u00e1nh for the Vietnamese pantheon.</div> </div> </div> </div>Added, thanks!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-29T10:18:11-07:00","id":1145283,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wickedgrail</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1145069-other-pantheon-names?p=1145162#post1145162\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> should they? if not Eskimo only refers to a race.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. All of these are names of pantheons. So I'm looking for the Inuit language word for &quot;gods&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-29T10:52:46-07:00","id":1145294,"title":"","content":"Adding the Aisar for the surviving Etruscan gods under Theoi rule.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-29T12:33:04-07:00","id":1145327,"title":"","content":"Wouldn't the Ossetian be the Narts? I'm pretty sure that term refers to the deities themselves and not just the sagas.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13079-wannabe-demon-lord","name":"Wannabe Demon Lord","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-29T12:46:38-07:00","id":1145331,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wannabe Demon Lord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1145069-other-pantheon-names?p=1145327#post1145327\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wouldn't the Ossetian be the Narts? I'm pretty sure that term refers to the deities themselves and not just the sagas.</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought the Narts was the term for the mortal heroes of said sagas.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-29T15:21:15-07:00","id":1145369,"title":"","content":"I think the Inuit are known as the Inue, are they not?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5627-purple-snit","name":"Purple Snit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5627_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"309"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-29T16:00:23-07:00","id":1145380,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Purple Snit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1145069-other-pantheon-names?p=1145369#post1145369\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the Inuit are known as the Inue, are they not?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I was reading debate over the authenticity of that term, but it may be the best option.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-30T06:58:36-07:00","id":1145514,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1145069-other-pantheon-names?p=1145283#post1145283\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes. All of these are names of pantheons. So I'm looking for the Inuit language word for &quot;gods&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Irish, egyptian, greek are not words that mean Gods... or do you mean words like Tuatha, Pesedjet, Dodekatheon?<br /> <br /> Edit: oh my, I got it.... haha","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1837-wickedgrail","name":"Wickedgrail","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1837_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-04T13:15:57-07:00","id":1146780,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Watcher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1145069-other-pantheon-names?p=1145081#post1145081\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is also the Hittite Pantheon who are the &quot;Thousand Gods of Hatti,&quot; who the Hittites regarded as a different group of Gods than their neighboring peoples worshiped such as the Egyptians and Akkadians. (though they totally nicked a lot of spare Deity-change off the Mesopotamians here and there) &quot;Shiunesh,&quot; is the term for a God too if that's helpful.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I'm finding Siwannes as a more common rendering than Shiunesh.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-04T13:51:56-07:00","id":1146793,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1145069-other-pantheon-names?p=1146780#post1146780\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm finding Siwannes as a more common rendering than Shiunesh.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah yeah! So, this is a whole thing. We know that is what GBN called the version of the Hittite Pantheon, but we couldn't track down exactly how on the nose that translation was. All of our sources use the term Shiunesh, we <i>think</i> it Siwannes might be an older translation? We could never track it down sadly. Are you finding the term Siwannes outside of GBN's version? If you have, we would really appreciate it if you let us know where you are seeing it so we can satisfy our curiosity about where they were getting the term.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-04T14:01:36-07:00","id":1146798,"title":"","content":"Only secondary sources, like here: <a href=\"https://books.google.com/books?id=gJjwCflv2q4C&amp;pg=PA358&amp;lpg=PA358&amp;dq=siwannes+gods&amp;source=bl&amp;ots=YIeLSS-6JF&amp;sig=k5Bu6jFHOsG5ILF02Q2IIaTopdc&amp;hl=en&amp;sa=X&amp;ved=0ahUKEwji3vye7tfWAhVI5GMKHbLWD1UQ6AEIOjAD#v=onepage&amp;q=siwannes%20gods&amp;f=false\" target=\"_blank\">https://books.google.com/books?id=gJ...20gods&amp;f=false</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-04T14:40:29-07:00","id":1146804,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1145069-other-pantheon-names?p=1146798#post1146798\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Only secondary sources, like here: <a href=\"https://books.google.com/books?id=gJjwCflv2q4C&amp;pg=PA358&amp;lpg=PA358&amp;dq=siwannes+gods&amp;source=bl&amp;ots=YIeLSS-6JF&amp;sig=k5Bu6jFHOsG5ILF02Q2IIaTopdc&amp;hl=en&amp;sa=X&amp;ved=0ahUKEwji3vye7tfWAhVI5GMKHbLWD1UQ6AEIOjAD#v=onepage&amp;q=siwannes%20gods&amp;f=false\" target=\"_blank\">https://books.google.com/books?id=gJ...20gods&amp;f=false</a></div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting, I wonder if the difference has to do with the fact it has an adjective attached to it.<br /> <br /> Hittite is particularly challenging to translate since it doesn't have an alphabet, it used Sumerograms. So, you have to transliterate from cuneiform to the Latin alphabet, something which is really challenging especially since the Hittites were putting their own spin on things IIRC. I have a feeling it might just be differences in how different scholars are transliterating the term, you can see by the two terms the disagreement is actually internally consistent. In our transliteration, the &quot;s&quot; sound of GBN's transliteration is being elongated into a &quot;sh&quot; sound. (<b>S</b>iwanne<b>s</b> = <b>Sh</b>iune<b>sh</b>) Both transliterations have an i after the first s/sh, and precede the final s/sh with an e. (S<b>i</b>wann<b>e</b>s = Sh<b>i</b>un<b>e</b>sh) Then the center of the word, &quot;wann&quot; and &quot;un&quot; is close to each other in sound.<br /> <br /> I'll double check with Sacerdos since he read the German side of the literature for the project since Germany is the main producer of academic work on the Hittites, and we are lucky that he can read German. I think it's a transliteration difference. There are a few times it shows up with some of the Deity names, and then in some cases, we <i>only</i> have the Sumerogram for an entity which makes things confusing. For example, the Hittites use the Sumerogram for &quot;Ea,&quot; for one of their own ancient primeval Gods, so we just have to call him Ea, even though he's not the same Ea of a few hundred kilometers to the east of their borders.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-04T15:18:46-07:00","id":1146824,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1145069-other-pantheon-names#post1145069\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Diwata - Philipinnes</div> </div> </div> </div>This one is mostly good, but there were a lot of pre-Spanish colonialism beliefs in the Philippines and one of those religious groups (the Palawan) used Diwata as the name of a specific deity so I'm not sure which group you're specifically referring to with this name but I think it might be better to refer to the individual pantheons by the groups that worshipped them such as the Tagalog or the Visayan, as opposed to using Diwata to cover the entirety of the Philipino mythology. This is based on my own general knowledge though so I don't know if you have a better source that pointed you at Diwata.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3653-thegraysoul","name":"TheGraySoul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"243"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-04T15:52:38-07:00","id":1146829,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheGraySoul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1145069-other-pantheon-names?p=1146824#post1146824\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This one is mostly good, but there were a lot of pre-Spanish colonialism beliefs in the Philippines and one of those religious groups (the Palawan) used Diwata as the name of a specific deity so I'm not sure which group you're specifically referring to with this name but I think it might be better to refer to the individual pantheons by the groups that worshipped them such as the Tagalog or the Visayan, as opposed to using Diwata to cover the entirety of the Philipino mythology. This is based on my own general knowledge though so I don't know if you have a better source that pointed you at Diwata.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Thanks, good note. I've been focusing on Tagalog legends because there seems to be most available to draw on. That said Bicolano legends, with Gugurang, Asuang, and Haliya, are really fascinating too - and I might see if I can find a distinct name for that pantheon too!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-04T16:17:08-07:00","id":1146834,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1145069-other-pantheon-names?p=1146829#post1146829\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks, good note. I've been focusing on Tagalog legends because there seems to be most available to draw on. That said Bicolano legends, with Gugurang, Asuang, and Haliya, are really fascinating too - and I might see if I can find a distinct name for that pantheon too!</div> </div> </div> </div>The T'Boli have some interesting stories too! Though I think there is significantly less information on their pantheon than the Tagalog.<br /> <a href=\"https://www.aswangproject.com/tboli-deities-myths/\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.aswangproject.com/tboli-deities-myths/</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3653-thegraysoul","name":"TheGraySoul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"243"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-04T17:16:37-07:00","id":1146857,"title":"","content":"For the Mapuche, I'd probably use Ngen (&quot;owner&quot;) who were the gods that dictated the order of the universe and the forces of nature. Either that or Pillan, who were considered benevolent spirits who combated the evil Wekufe, or evil spirits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/267-griffinguy24","name":"griffinguy24","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar267_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-04T17:56:02-07:00","id":1146870,"title":"","content":"Ngen definitely works, with Pillan and Wekufe being internal camps.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-04T22:37:11-07:00","id":1146912,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1145069-other-pantheon-names?p=1146780#post1146780\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm finding Siwannes as a more common rendering than Shiunesh.</div> </div> </div> </div>Both are different transliterations of the same thing. Leaving the \u0161 as s is academic custom, but it should still be spoken as &quot;sh&quot;-sound, so I prefer to transliterate it as sh right away. The u instead of wa is totally coming from me using, like Watcher mentioned, German scholarship, where this mode of transliteration is more usual; for example, we would also transliterate the Egyptian god you know as Wepwawet as Upuaut. Due to the importance of German scholarship in Hittite studies, I have seen many English-language works as well follow this mode of transliteration; frankly, the link you provided is the first time I saw &quot;siwannes&quot; used in an academic work. So, good to know this form of transliteration <i>is </i>used after all, but we'll stick with ours. I find that this mode better strikes the balance between accurate and readable, and it is what I'm used to from the uni courses I took on the Hittites. But in the end, your list is good with both.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10624-sacerdos","name":"Sacerdos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10624_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"231"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-05T05:43:35-07:00","id":1146985,"title":"","content":"One of the most recent &quot;Pantheon&quot; is Wicca. What is their people since it's a little bit everywhere: Canada, USA, UK. ? I'm trying to make a Pantheon out of this. I've thought to call them simply Witches, for both male and female (yeah, something like what Charmed did).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1837-wickedgrail","name":"Wickedgrail","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1837_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-05T05:55:20-07:00","id":1146991,"title":"","content":"Witches is accurately gender neutral (it was only feminized because of Early Modern Witch-Hunters being as misogynist as they were) but it doesn\u2019t really apply to deities.<br /> <br /> Generally Wiccans draw eclectically from various pantheons, treating different divinities as faces of \u201cGoddess\u201d and \u201cGod\u201d, rather than having a defined deity mythos of their own.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-06T04:58:57-07:00","id":1147369,"title":"","content":"If you use Shen/Kami for the Chinese/Japanese pantheon then the Vietnamese one should be Th\u1ea7n, since it's the most common word to refer to gods (back when Vietnam still used the Chinese script, th\u1ea7n is how we pronounce the character \u795e).<br /> <br /> Th\u00e1nh means someone who is holy/virtuous/wise, though nowadays it has a more Christianity flavor and is usually used for saint.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-06T05:37:15-07:00","id":1147379,"title":"","content":"Thanks, I\u2019ll adjust accordingly!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-06T08:26:40-07:00","id":1147434,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1145069-other-pantheon-names?p=1146991#post1146991\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Witches is accurately gender neutral (it was only feminized because of Early Modern Witch-Hunters being as misogynist as they were) but it doesn\u2019t really apply to deities.<br /> <br /> Generally Wiccans draw eclectically from various pantheons, treating different divinities as faces of \u201cGoddess\u201d and \u201cGod\u201d, rather than having a defined deity mythos of their own.</div> </div> </div> </div>True, but from all those antique Pantheons, Wicca is the most up to date. They would have more followers than any Greek Gods or Aztec gods for example. <br /> <br /> They borrow other Gods but maybe that's the new way for ancient gods to be still believed: joining forces to create a new general pantheon where we pray for the God or the Goddess we wish to interact with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1837-wickedgrail","name":"Wickedgrail","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1837_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-06T10:22:02-07:00","id":1147480,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wickedgrail</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1145069-other-pantheon-names?p=1147434#post1147434\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> True, but from all those antique Pantheons, Wicca is the most up to date. They would have more followers than any Greek Gods or Aztec gods for example. <br /> <br /> They borrow other Gods but maybe that's the new way for ancient gods to be still believed: joining forces to create a new general pantheon where we pray for the God or the Goddess we wish to interact with.</div> </div> </div> </div>Right, but that\u2019s a polyglot way to interact with various gods, not a new roster of gods. What gods would be in the \u201cWiccan Pantheon\u201d that aren\u2019t in other pantheons?<br /> <br /> I\u2019m inclined to interpret Wicca in \u201cthe World\u201d (a setting where the Old Faiths Wicca is reconstructed from never died out in the first place) as a religious tradition specifically notable for its open relationship toward gods of diverse Pantheons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 10-06-2017, 01:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-29T14:09:32-07:00","id":1153982,"title":"","content":"Some More:<br /> Anito- Bicolano<br /> Hesaketvmese- Muscogee<br /> Ipmil- Sami<br /> Jainko- Basque<br /> Kamuy- Ainu<br /> Khoikhoi- Khoisan (They seem to use the same word in their language for deities as they do for themselves.)<br /> Lubaale- Bunyoro<br /> Maha-Andriamnitra- Malagasy<br /> Mulungu- Nyanga<br /> Narts- Ossetian (Having done more research, the Narts are definitely divine. Not all the deities are referred to as Narts, but the generation the epics focus on are.)<br /> Nunne'hi- Cherokee<br /> Orenda- Iroquois<br /> Shilombish- Choctaw<br /> Tupa- Tupi<br /> Uungu- Mbuti (The Mbuti speak Swahili, and that's the Swahili word for deity.)<br /> <br /> I got this from about an hour of googling, so I'm not absolutely certain it's accurate, so if someone corrects this they're probably right","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13079-wannabe-demon-lord","name":"Wannabe Demon Lord","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-29T14:23:36-07:00","id":1153986,"title":"","content":"I'm going to draw a distinction between the &quot;Numina&quot; - who are older Sabine gods adopted by the Romans (the most important one of prominence is Janus), and the &quot;Di Indigetes&quot;, who are ascended Roman-born Scions of the Theoi. Quirinus straddles both groups as Romulus, Scion of Mars, is clearly Di Indigetes, but he assumed the Mantle of an older Sabine war god he slew.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-29T14:33:22-07:00","id":1153988,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wannabe Demon Lord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1145069-other-pantheon-names?p=1153982#post1153982\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some More:<br /> Anito- Bicolano<br /> Hesaketvmese- Muscogee<br /> Ipmil- Sami<br /> Jainko- Basque<br /> Kamuy- Ainu<br /> Khoikhoi- Khoisan (They seem to use the same word in their language for deities as they do for themselves.)<br /> Lubaale- Bunyoro<br /> Maha-Andriamnitra- Malagasy<br /> Mulungu- Nyanga<br /> Narts- Ossetian (Having done more research, the Narts are definitely divine. Not all the deities are referred to as Narts, but the generation the epics focus on are.)<br /> Nunne'hi- Cherokee<br /> Orenda- Iroquois<br /> Shilombish- Choctaw<br /> Tupa- Tupi<br /> Uungu- Mbuti (The Mbuti speak Swahili, and that's the Swahili word for deity.)<br /> <br /> I got this from about an hour of googling, so I'm not absolutely certain it's accurate, so if someone corrects this they're probably right</div> </div> </div> </div>Adding several of these, thanks! Some I'm still digging on because I want to make sure they aren't SPECIFICALLY the singular name for a supreme deity, but also refer to divinities in the plural.<br /> <br /> For example, it appears &quot;Mulungu&quot; is specifically the singular name of the Supreme Deity that is used in Bantu translations of the Bible and Qu'ran - while &quot;Milungu&quot; is the plural that incorporates ancestor divinities.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-25T07:38:42-08:00","id":1189396,"title":"","content":"Vairgit- Chukchee<br /> Ichchi- Yakut<br /> Enduri- Manchu<br /> Yakush- Berber<br /> Niwaskow8gan- Wabanaki<br /> Disa- Thracian","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13079,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13079-wannabe-demon-lord","user":"Wannabe Demon Lord","date":". 02-28-2018, 07:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13079-wannabe-demon-lord","name":"Wannabe Demon Lord","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}